# ── Repo-specific ──
## Large build artifacts - keep folders via .gitkeep
libs/**
libs/*
libs/
## EXCEPTION: 1_workflows/src/libs/ is engine source code, NOT build artifacts.
## Same convention as the cloud repo. Added 2026-05-16 after the engine broke
## because inject-header.sh was ignored despite being referenced by build.sh.
!1_workflows/src/libs/
!1_workflows/src/libs/**
## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-superapp/libs/ is the gradle multi-module source tree
## (libs:core, libs:mail, libs:cal, …). Each is its own Android library
## with build.gradle + src/. NOT build artifacts. Added 2026-05-29 when
## the scaffold landed and these files silently disappeared on git add;
## renamed from ea_superapp → ea_cloud-superapp 2026-05-30.
!ea_cloud-superapp/libs/
!ea_cloud-superapp/libs/**
## Upstream tracking clones (workspace-only — never vendored).
## Pattern: ea_<domain>-<project>/ holds a shallow clone of the upstream
## FOSS app we're cherry-picking into ea_cloud-superapp/libs/<domain>/.
## Today: ea_mail-fairmail (FairEmail, GPLv3), ea_cal-davx5 (DAVx5, GPLv3),
## ea_feed-feeder (Feeder, GPLv3), ea_net-wireguard (wireguard-android,
## Apache-2.0), ea_vault-keepassdx (KeePassDX, GPLv3). Each is refreshed
## with `git -C ea_<x>-<y> pull` independently.
ea_*-*/
## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-superapp/ itself owns a `-` in its directory name
## (renamed from ea_superapp 2026-05-30 to match the Cloud SuperApp brand).
## Whitelist the whole subtree — the rule above is for shallow upstream
## clones (FairEmail, DAVx5, …), NOT for our owned modules.
!ea_cloud-superapp/
!ea_cloud-superapp/**
## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-comms/ — the Cloud-Comms constellation project
## (hub APK + declarative fork patch-series for FairEmail/Mattermost/
## Element X). Owns a `-` so it matches the ea_*-*/ ignore above; whitelist
## the whole owned subtree exactly like ea_cloud-superapp. The forks
## themselves are NOT vendored — they materialize at build time into
## ea_chat-mattermost/ + ea_chat-element/ + the existing ea_mail-fairmail/
## tracker clones, which stay ignored by the ea_*-*/ rule. Added 2026-06-11.
!ea_cloud-comms/
!ea_cloud-comms/**
## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-ide/ — the Cloud-IDE constellation project (twin of
## ea_cloud-comms): hub APK + declarative fork patch-series for Acode /
## Amaze File Manager / Amaze File Utilities. Owns a `-` so it matches the
## ea_*-*/ ignore above; whitelist the whole owned subtree exactly like
## ea_cloud-comms. The forks themselves are NOT vendored — they materialize at
## build time into ea_upstreams-sources/{editor-acode,files-amaze,
## files-amaze-utils}/ tracker clones (the same inventory dir the superapp
## upstreams live in), content ignored by the ea_*-*/ rule. Added 2026-06-11;
## trackers moved into ea_upstreams-sources/ 2026-06-12.
!ea_cloud-ide/
!ea_cloud-ide/**
## EXCEPTION: ea_cloud-nav/ — dedicated maps/navigation/tracker app. libs:maps
## (MapLibre renderer + GPS tracker + Timeline + MyTrips) was lifted OUT of
## ea_cloud-superapp into its own modularized-monolith APK. Owns a `-` so it
## matches the ea_*-*/ ignore above; whitelist the whole owned subtree exactly
## like ea_cloud-superapp / ea_cloud-comms / ea_cloud-ide. Added 2026-06-14.
!ea_cloud-nav/
!ea_cloud-nav/**
## Re-ignore signing keystores inside the whitelisted Android projects. The
## !ea_cloud-*/** whitelists above would otherwise override the *.jks/*.keystore
## rules (lines ~27-28) and make a locally-generated keystore committable.
## Keystores are generated in CI (actions/cache) only — never vendored. Added
## 2026-06-11 (closes the latent gap for superapp + comms + ide alike).
ea_cloud-superapp/**/*.keystore
ea_cloud-superapp/**/*.jks
ea_cloud-comms/**/*.keystore
ea_cloud-comms/**/*.jks
ea_cloud-ide/**/*.keystore
ea_cloud-ide/**/*.jks
ea_cloud-nav/**/*.keystore
ea_cloud-nav/**/*.jks
## Re-ignore Gradle build outputs inside the whitelisted ea_cloud-ide/ tree
## (the !ea_cloud-ide/** whitelist would otherwise track build/.gradle dirs).
## Added 2026-06-13.
ea_cloud-ide/.gradle/
ea_cloud-ide/build/
ea_cloud-ide/**/build/
ea_cloud-nav/.gradle/
ea_cloud-nav/build/
ea_cloud-nav/**/build/
## Re-ignore build OUTPUTS inside the whitelisted Android projects — the
## !ea_cloud-*/** whitelists would otherwise make a locally-built APK / dist/
## tree committable (each APK is ~6-40 MB). Build artifacts are published to
## GHCR + GH Releases by the ship workflows, never vendored in git.
ea_cloud-superapp/dist/
ea_cloud-superapp/**/*.apk
ea_cloud-comms/dist/
ea_cloud-comms/**/*.apk
ea_cloud-ide/dist/
ea_cloud-ide/**/*.apk
ea_cloud-nav/dist/
ea_cloud-nav/**/*.apk
## MyShell bundled nix store (500MB+)
ba_myshell/dist/*/_bundled/
ba_myshell/bin/
## Container storage
storage/
!storage/.gitkeep
